      "message": "[error] Line 64: 🔴 `push()` now holds `state_-\u003emutex` while calling `updateFpsTracker()` and emitting `frameUpdated()`. This is a behavioral regression from the previous code (which unlocked before notifications) and can deadlock if any direct-connected slot re-enters renderer paths that also take `state_-\u003emutex` (or blocks teardown waiting on that path). Keep the critical section limited to `parent`/`frameBufferPtr` access, then release the lock before calling into Qt signals or other parent methods; use a guarded parent handle (e.g., `QPointer`) captured under lock to avoid use-after-free.",
